 They carry _breath_ to the dead — __“Come from the four winds, O breath… that they may live”__ (Ezekiel 37:9).
 Scatter and gather, stir and raise: the wind’s direction is set by its Sender, not by itself.
 
-The gathering has an address: the elect are collected __“from the *four winds*, from one end of heaven to the other”__ — from the four _corners_ of the earth where the dispersed wait (Isaiah 11:12), corners the link:/books/symbolic-language/wings/[Wings] chapter searched; the winds sweep the quarters, and the quarters give up their gleanings.
+from the four _corners_ of the earth where the dispersed wait (Isaiah 11:12), corners that the link:/books/symbolic-language/wings/[Wings] chapter searched; the winds sweep the quarters, and the quarters give up their gleanings.
 
 The judgment-wind even has a compass habit.
 It was __“a strong sym:sym-east[east] *wind*”__ that split the sea all night (Exodus 14:21); an east wind carried in the locusts (Exodus 10:13); a __“vehement east wind”__ broke Jonah (Jonah 4:8); and Hosea names whose wind it is: __“an *east wind* shall come, *the wind of the LORD*… and his spring shall become dry”__ (Hosea 13:15).
